/*
 * Post Parade Adventure 2: the six stages, drawn. Generated by tools/genstages.py -- draw a
 * stage there, not here.
 *
 * Each stage is one runner's own ground, as Sonic Battle gives each fighter a home arena:
 * Sonic's seaside, Tails' workshop, Amy's home, Knuckles' shrines in the snow, Rouge's club,
 * Shadow's highway. Each is chunks of text, 32 rows each, laid side by side: one character a
 * one-metre tile, the top row first. adventure.js reads them (parse) and builds them in
 * voxels. The ground mostly stands on row 27, so a runner's feet are four metres up; a jump
 * clears two rows, a spring about six, an updraft eight or more.
 *
 *   .  air                    #  ground (grass, a rug, rock, carpet, road: the theme says)
 *   =  the theme's blocks (stone, steel, books, carved stone, neon glass, concrete)
 *   /  \  slopes, rising right / falling right
 *   -  a ledge: jump up through it, stand on it, Down + jump to drop through
 *   {  }  a conveyor belt, running left / right
 *   ~  water                  I  ice (slippery)          m  mud (slow)
 *   X  cracked rock: any move breaks it (a kick, a spin, a drill)
 *   B  crate: breaks the same way, or from below, and lets out three carrots
 *   C  a ledge that crumbles a moment after it is stood on, and comes back
 *   ^  thorns                 S  spring                  >  dash strip
 *   M  a plank that slides (a run of them is one plank)    V  one that rises and falls
 *   U  an updraft             O  an air vent under water
 *   Q  a bumper               o  a balloon: pops, and throws you up
 *   c  carrot   J  carrot juice (a heart)   *  rainbow carrot (eight seconds untouchable)
 *   H  a Golden Horseshoe -- three to a stage
 *   k r b n p  badniks: which, the stage's theme says (THEMES.foes in adventure.js)
 *   h  a hurdle: jump it, or smash it (a brush fence, a barrier, books, a cairn, a rope)
 *   P  start   K  furlong pole (a checkpoint)   G  the winning post   T  something behind
 *
 * `who` is the runner whose ground it is; `par` the time an S grade has to beat; `was` the
 * stage it took the place of, whose clear still opens it.
 */
